abstract: >-
  This MATLAB package aims to determine what is Warm Deep
  Water, how does it enter the Weddell gyre, and how the
  main advective pathways result in its modification and
  formation. To do this, we define UCDW as Tmax and dO2min,
  and LCDW as Smax and map the results, using gridded mean
  fields from WOA, and also ungridded Argo floats. Along
  selected streamlines downloaded from
  https://doi.pangaea.de/10.1594/PANGAEA.960571, we
  determine the long-term mean variation of Tmax, Smax and
  dO2min throughout the gyre. This work is presented in
  Reeve et al. (2026) submitted to Geophysical Research
  Letters and generates the complete data analyses and
  figures for the manuscript. 
